cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Silicon Atlas: interactive labs for semiconductor materials and devices"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Sean
    affiliation: "Princeton University, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering"
version: 0.9.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sean-KSH/silicon-atlas"
url: "https://sean-ksh.github.io/silicon-atlas/"
abstract: >-
  Ten interactive, model-backed teaching modules covering silicon purification and crystal growth,
  crystal structure and bands, equilibrium carrier statistics, carrier transport, a metal-gate nMOS
  fabrication flow, p-n junction electrostatics, diode current, MOS capacitors and MOSFETs,
  photonic devices, and a virtual measurement bench.
keywords:
  - semiconductor devices
  - physics education
  - simulation
